1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,396
Razorface: a priest of pain in a face full of nails, and he has come to collect.

2
00:00:04,616 --> 00:00:05,896
Here's how he plays.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,839
Shuffle the eight Affliction cards, draw three and lay them face up.

4
00:00:09,839 --> 00:00:11,777
Those are the hellish chains on your soul.

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,747
To kill Razorface you must first purge every Affliction you have.

6
00:00:15,747 --> 00:00:18,168
Usually that's three, but cards can give you more.

7
00:00:18,388 --> 00:00:22,291
Each Affliction has a Purge Requirement on top, and a Purge Effect on the bottom

8
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:23,999
that you resolve when you purge it.

9
00:00:24,219 --> 00:00:28,588
For example, The Gift of Pain: deal at least three damage to Razorface in one Action

10
00:00:28,588 --> 00:00:30,512
phase. Do that, and you can purge it.

11
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:35,156
During the Action phase, if you've met an Affliction's requirement, you may purge

12
00:00:35,156 --> 00:00:38,224
it: resolve its Purge Effect, then remove the card from the game.

13
00:00:38,444 --> 00:00:42,667
If you choose not to, the requirement has to be met again later before you can purge

14
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:42,817
it.

15
00:00:43,037 --> 00:00:46,231
And you can only purge one Affliction per turn, so start early.

16
00:00:46,231 --> 00:00:48,157
Leaving them all to the end is a trap.

17
00:00:48,967 --> 00:00:53,180
Sometimes an Affliction becomes impossible, for example one that needs a Victim when

18
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:54,535
none are left on the board.

19
00:00:54,755 --> 00:00:57,421
Remove it from the game and draw a new one to replace it.

20
00:00:57,641 --> 00:01:01,545
If you ever need to draw an Affliction and the deck is empty, you lose immediately.

21
00:01:02,367 --> 00:01:07,017
Razorface's Final Health token can only be revealed when no Afflictions are in play.

22
00:01:07,237 --> 00:01:11,243
If he's down to his Final Health token and you still have an Affliction, any damage

23
00:01:11,243 --> 00:01:13,125
that would reveal it is simply ignored.

24
00:01:13,345 --> 00:01:17,212
So you can wear him down first, but the killing blow only lands after your last

25
00:01:17,212 --> 00:01:17,505
purge.

26
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:20,893
Soulbound: when it's revealed, you gain a new Affliction.

27
00:01:21,113 --> 00:01:25,336
Helleport lets him kill a Victim wherever they are, and Life Drain is his deadliest

28
00:01:25,336 --> 00:01:28,388
power: players win under half their games when it comes out.

29
00:01:28,608 --> 00:01:32,518
His Epic Dark Power, Infinite Despair, punishes you every Panic phase:

30
00:01:32,518 --> 00:01:36,261
one effect if at least one Victim panicked, a different one if not.

31
00:01:36,261 --> 00:01:40,171
The card shows the amounts as icons; expect Horror to rise every turn.

32
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,329
Sadistic Manifestation places Razorface with the farthest Victim, then targets a

33
00:01:45,329 --> 00:01:49,875
Victim and attacks twice. If there are no Victims on the board, draw the next Terror

34
00:01:49,875 --> 00:01:50,579
card instead.

35
00:01:50,799 --> 00:01:55,130
One Affliction, Experience Unbound, heals Razorface three health when you purge it,

36
00:01:55,130 --> 00:01:57,583
so purge that one before you start hurting him.

37
00:01:57,803 --> 00:02:02,279
His Minor Dark Powers, The Pain of Judgement and The Pain of Salvation, make him

38
00:02:02,279 --> 00:02:05,077
kill Victims more easily and punish Focus actions.

39
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:10,164
Chains of Torment: each Killer phase he targets a Victim, moves and attacks twice,

40
00:02:10,164 --> 00:02:14,324
and whenever he enters a space with at least one Victim, the effect shown on the

41
00:02:14,324 --> 00:02:15,052
card triggers.

42
00:02:15,272 --> 00:02:19,277
I Feast on Your Pain attacks twice with a bonus based on Bloodlust, and Taste Our

43
00:02:19,277 --> 00:02:21,501
Pleasures is the most dangerous of the three.

44
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:26,571
A few tips. You can only purge one Affliction a turn, so start in turn one and keep

45
00:02:26,571 --> 00:02:26,877
going.

46
00:02:27,097 --> 00:02:30,233
Purge any Affliction that heals him before you start dealing damage.

47
00:02:30,453 --> 00:02:34,016
And he's one of the tougher killers: players win just over half their games.

48
00:02:34,016 --> 00:02:34,485
Good luck.

